Declarative example:
```groovy
pipeline {
  agent { docker { image 'node:20' } }
  stages {
    stage('Test') {
      steps { sh 'npm test' }
    }
    stage('Deploy') {
      when { branch 'main' }
      steps { sh './deploy.sh' }
    }
  }
  post { failure { mail to: 'team@x.com' } }
}
```

Scripted example:
```groovy
node('linux') {
  stage('Test') {
    checkout scm
    sh 'npm test'
  }
  if (env.BRANCH_NAME == 'main') {
    stage('Deploy') { sh './deploy.sh' }
  }
}
```

Declarative features: (a) 'agent' — where to run. (b) 'stages' — sequential. (c) 'steps' — inside stage. (d) 'when' — conditional stage. (e) 'post' — always/success/failure/etc. (f) 'options' — retry, timeout. (g) 'environment' — env vars. (h) 'parameters' — inputs.

Escape hatch: 'script { }' block dentro de declarative permite Groovy libre para lógica compleja. Usar sparingly — hint de refactor.

Shared libraries: extract common logic. En src/, vars/. Import con '@Library'. Enables 'as-code' pipeline patterns across teams.

Blue Ocean UI: visualiza pipelines declaratives mejor que scripted. Motivador para migrar.

Anti-patrones: (1) Massive scripted Jenkinsfile — 2000 lines Groovy. Fix: shared libraries + declarative. (2) Logic outside pipeline in Jenkins UI (hidden config). Fix: move to Jenkinsfile. (3) No agent specified — uses master (bad practice, master reserved for orchestration).
